You are helping build Rumbo — a Tauri 2 + React + TypeScript desktop app 
for college students with attentional learning differences.

Always read RUMBO_SPEC.md before suggesting architecture or new files.
Always use the types defined in types.ts — never redefine interfaces that already exist.

The scheduling algorithm is deterministic TypeScript — never suggest calling 
an AI API for scheduling, classification, or profile updates.

The only AI calls in the entire app are:
1. parse-pdf edge function (premium, PDF upload)
2. parse-description edge function (premium, task description)

The app has two windows:
1. Quick-add modal — always-on-top, triggered by tray icon or hotkey
2. Main dashboard — standard window, opened from tray menu

Entry point is the system tray icon, not a hotkey. Global hotkey is secondary.

Tech stack: Tauri 2 + Rust core, React 18, TypeScript, Vite, 
Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Zustand, TanStack Query, Supabase.